Changes:
- templates/show_lldp_neighbors_detail.textfsm: renamed from arista_eos_show_lldp_neighbors_detail.textfsm.
- templates/show_interfaces_status.textfsm: renamed from arista_eos_show_interfaces_status.textfsm;
  the NAME value `(\S.*(?<!\s))` became `(\S.*\S|\S)`, because Go regular expressions have no
  lookbehind.
- templates/show_lldp_neighbors_detail.textfsm: added the MGMT_ADDRESS_SUBTYPE value, so the
  management address is stored with its LLDP subtype.
- testdata/ntc/show_lldp_neighbors_detail.yml: each row gained mgmt_address_subtype, read from the
  "Management Address Subtype" line of the same neighbour in the .raw file.
- testdata/ntc/: test fixtures renamed without the arista_eos_ prefix.
- templates/show_interfaces.textfsm: renamed from arista_eos_show_interfaces.textfsm; the
  INTERFACE value became PORT, so the interfaces recipe maps the port of both its steps with one
  name. The Fallback rule also accepts "Fallback timeout is N seconds", which EOS prints on a
  port-channel with LACP fallback and the upstream template rejects.
  The catch-all rule for lines starting with a number takes one word after it instead of two, so
  a VXLAN flood list line ("40 10.0.255.13") no longer fails the parse.
- testdata/ntc/show_interfaces*.yml: the interface key became port, to match the template.
